---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import GetChip from '../components/GetChip.astro';
---
<Shell
  current="relay"
  title="Relay — SIERRA gateways · The Grid"
  description="SIERRA's own MeshCore gateways and whether each can be used right now, live from the mesh relay's public status, GET /mesh/relay/api/status."
>
  <!-- is:global: the rows are built at runtime by relay.js. Same row tints as
       the Sources board, from the canonical --st-* ramp. -->
  <style is:global slot="head">
    #relay-board .data-table tr.row-STALE { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--st-STALE) 8%, transparent); }
    #relay-board .data-table tr.row-UNAVAILABLE { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--st-UNAVAILABLE) 11%, transparent); }
  </style>

  <PageHead kicker="Mesh relay" title="Relay">
    <p class="lead">SIERRA's own gateways, and whether each can be used now.</p>
    <GetChip slot="badges" path="/mesh/relay/api/status" />
  </PageHead>

  <p class="rail-caption">
    <b>Board</b>one row per gateway, least usable first · state → node → lease → bridge → last
    seen · served by the mesh relay, a separate service from the rest of this API
  </p>

  <!-- Sidenotes, not a rail: the board is a six-column table (the Sources
       reasoning). -->
  <div class="with-notes">
    <p class="section-intro">
      A gateway is a MeshCore companion radio at a volunteer's house, plus a bridge program that
      dials out to the relay. Authorized operators and agents reach a node through it, one session
      at a time.
      <span class="accent-orange">If the relay does not answer, gateway status is unknown, which
      is not the same as every gateway being offline.</span>
    </p>
    <aside class="sidenote">
      <div class="rail-label">Reading the board</div>
      <p>
        <span class="mono">READY</span>: the bridge is online and its radio is connected and
        verified. <span class="mono">NODE DOWN</span>: the bridge is online but its radio is not.
        <span class="mono">UNVERIFIED</span>: the radio reports a different key than the one on
        record, so nobody can use it until an admin accepts the change.
        <span class="mono">OFFLINE</span>: no bridge is attached.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <div id="relay-summary" class="chip-row" aria-live="polite"></div>
  <div id="relay-errors"></div>
  <div id="relay-board"></div>
  <p id="relay-refresh" class="freshness"></p>

  <div class="with-notes section-gap">
    <p class="section-intro">
      This board says whether a gateway works, and nothing else. It never shows where a gateway is,
      who is using one, or a node's key or name: those would point at a volunteer's house, or say
      when a particular person is on the mesh.
      For the mesh the gateways serve, see <a href="/mesh">Mesh</a>.
    </p>
    <aside class="sidenote">
      <div class="rail-label">Using a gateway</div>
      <p>
        A session needs a client token issued by a SIERRA admin. <span class="mono">in use</span>
        means someone holds the gateway's one session, with the kind of client beside it
        (<span class="mono">agent</span>, <span class="mono">operator</span> or
        <span class="mono">admin</span>), never who. It frees up when they disconnect, after 10
        minutes idle, or when the session expires.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <script is:inline type="module">
    import { initRelayPage } from '/assets/pages/relay.js';
    initRelayPage();
  </script>
</Shell>
